---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About the practice | Techno War Room"
  description="Techno War Room is a commercial pursuit practice: we run the proposals, decks, questionnaires, and pricing inside must-win deals for B2B SaaS and IT services firms."
>
  <header class="svc-hero">
    <span class="band-top" style="background:var(--cobalt)"></span>
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> ⚡ About</nav>
      <span class="kicker">The practice ⚡ Not a team page</span>
      <h1>A war room <span class="hollow-ink">you can hire.</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Techno War Room is a commercial pursuit practice. When a deal that matters lands, we run the work it generates: the response, the deck, the answers, the pricing, and the proof.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-tag">01 / The practice</span><h2>What this <span class="u">is</span></h2></div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Sales organisations at B2B SaaS and IT services firms carry more live pursuits than qualified people to run them. The deals still arrive: the three hundred question RFP, the committee presentation, the security questionnaire, the pricing rebuild. The material has to be excellent precisely when everyone is busiest.</p>
        <p>We exist to absorb that spike. One firm, engaged for one pursuit at a time, doing the commercial work at the standard the deal deserves. Your team stays in front of the buyer. We carry the documents.</p>
        <p>This page describes a practice rather than people, on purpose. What you are hiring is a way of working, and the way of working is written down here and demonstrated across this site.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-tag">02 / The method</span><h2>How we <span class="u">work</span></h2></div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step"><span class="n">1</span><h3>Must-win only</h3><p>We take deals that matter and decline the routine ones. Focus is the product.</p></div>
        <div class="step s-mustard"><span class="n">2</span><h3>Scoped to the pursuit</h3><p>Engagements have a start, a submission date, and an end. Then we hand the room back.</p></div>
        <div class="step s-cyan"><span class="n">3</span><h3>Invisible to the buyer</h3><p>Your templates, your tools, your voice. The buyer only ever sees your firm.</p></div>
        <div class="step s-red"><span class="n">4</span><h3>Nothing invented</h3><p>No fabricated claims, metrics, or answers. If a fact is missing, we say so and write the mitigation.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-tag">03 / The beliefs</span><h2>What we believe about <span class="ur">pursuits</span></h2></div>
      <div style="max-width:760px">
        <div class="belief">
          <h3>Deals are lost in documents more often than in meetings.</h3>
          <p>The committee reads alone. The compliance matrix gets checked. The SOW ambiguity surfaces in month six. The written material is the deal, long after the meeting charm fades.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="belief">
          <h3>The losing margin is usually small and usually fixable.</h3>
          <p>A missed requirement, a thin answer, a deck with no argument. Seven figure outcomes turn on work that a focused week would have fixed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="belief">
          <h3>Quality should not depend on who happened to be free.</h3>
          <p>Most bid teams staff pursuits with whoever is available that month. A war room exists so the standard is the same on every deal, including the one that lands on a Friday evening.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="belief">
          <h3>Honesty is a competitive weapon.</h3>
          <p>An honest gap with a written mitigation beats a hopeful yes in every evaluation that matters, because buyers check. Our own site follows the same rule: no invented clients, no invented numbers.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta-box">
        <span class="sticker cta-stk">No charge to talk</span>
        <h2>Got a live one?</h2>
        <p>If there is a deal on the table, we can tell you quickly whether we can help and what it would involve.</p>
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Book a call</a>
        <svg class="cta-brick" viewBox="-60 0 240 220" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#brickhero"></use></svg>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
